    "summary": "Root cause: dec:girder.A had been accepted with the single-girder area (1.1389 m²) instead of the total area of the merged precast section. Per MR-02 a precast spine-beam model must use A = A_single × n_girders = 1.13893 × 3 = 3.41679 m². This inconsistency made girder.w (MR-07) recompute as 26×1.1389 = 29.61 kN/m while the stored/model value was 88.84 kN/m, and made the L3-2 engineering-quantity total weight (γ·A·L) disagree with the model self-weight.\n\nRepair: re-proposed girder.A = 3.41679 m² (MR-02), re-proposed girder.w = 88.836 kN/m (= 26 × 3.41679, MR-07) and girder.m = 9.0557 t/m (w/g). girder.I (1.06475 m²) was already correct (1 × 3). Re-ran the modal analysis: f1 = 3.402 Hz unchanged, so lane.mu = 0.1767·ln(f1) − 0.0157 = 0.20063 (JTG D60-2015 4.3.2) remained valid. generate_model then passed all L1/L2/L3 checks.\n\nFinal model: single simply-supported 30 m span, spine-beam 2D, 3 C40 precast small-box girders merged to A = 3.4168 m², I = 1.06475 m⁴, Ec = 32.5 GPa, γ = 26 kN/m³, w = 88.84 kN/m, m = 9.056 t/m; plain laminated elastomeric bearings (300×400, 5×8 mm layers) at both abutments, 6 per line, spring vertical/longitudinal restraint; Class-II lane load with μ = 0.2006. Results: f1 = 3.402 Hz; self-weight reactions 1332.5 kN per abutment; self-weight midspan moment 9994.1 kNm; lane-load max positive moment 6449.6 kNm."
